      "side": 1,
      "message": "Furthermore, as mentioned on the linked bug, this doesn\u0027t actually work correctly:\n\nNot dropping FIN doesn\u0027t mean we won\u0027t drop the ACK that it in turn generates, which means the FIN will *still* be retransmitted.\n\n-\u003e SYN\n\u003c- SYN/ACK\n-\u003e ACK\n\nestablished\n\ndoze enabled\n\none side terminates connection, sends FIN, it now passes through the rules\n(if it\u0027s us generating FIN, we just woke the modem/wifi chip up)\n\nthe reply ACK is *NOT* (necessarily) FIN marked and is thus still dropped by the rules\n\nFIN gets resent a few times, if it was us sending it in the first place... we wake the modem/wifi chip up a few more times to rexmit it",
      "revId": "8ec0fc42f8e28c5ee3b74f94c66265b83bc39702",
